[38;2;124;124;124mFor any $B \in \mathcal{U}$ and any $\{B_i\}_{i \in B}$ with $B_i \in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathcal{U}$, the set $\bigcup_{i \in B} \varphi_i(B_i) \in \mathcal{U}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think about what this means. Each $\varphi_i$ is a bijection $\omega \to [0m[38;2;124;124;124mS_i$. Think of $\varphi_i$ as "transporting" the ultrafilter structure. If we [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mthink of each $S_i$ as a copy of $\omega$ via $\varphi_i$, then $\varphi_i(B_i)$[0m[38;2;124;124;124mis the "image" of the big set $B_i$ inside $S_i$.[0m

